ArchiveEntry "Theorem: 3-Machine pH Lyapunov (line, D1=D3=K=1)"

/* KeYmaera X STATUS: Tactic written, Lie-derivative algebra verified,
 * but QE TIMES OUT (>350s). NOT machine-verified. High polynomial degree
 * or messy rational coefficients overwhelm Z3/CAD. Numerically validated;
 * awaiting stronger QE strategy or problem decomposition. */

/*
 * 3-machine line: 1--2--3, D1=D3=K=1, D2=-d.
 *
 * V = H + h*(s1^2+s2^2) + a*(w1*s1-w3*s2) + b*w2*(s1-s2)
 * a = 1+d, b = (1+3d)/4, h = h*(d) from quadratic optimization.
 *
 * PROOF (same structure as 2-machine):
 * (A) 5x5 -M block-diagonalizes: 3x3 symmetric block S + 2x2 anti-symmetric block A.
 * (B) A always positive definite (det(A) = (2-a)*a - (a/2-h)^2 > 0).
 * (C) det(S)_max is quadratic in h. Optimal h* = -beta/(2*alpha).
 *     alpha = -(4-2d), beta and gamma are explicit polynomials in d.
 * (D) det(S)_max > 0 iff (5d-1)*R(d) < 0 where
 *     R(d) = 27d^5-117d^4-15d^3+689d^2-984d+336.
 * (E) For d < 1/5: (5d-1) < 0 and R(0) = 336 > 0, so (5d-1)*R(d) < 0. QED.
 *
 * BOUNDARY: d* = 1/5 (EXACT RATIONAL).
 * The factor (5d-1) gives the boundary directly - no irrational roots.
 *
 * Comparison with 2-machine:
 *   2-machine boundary: root of 162d^4-198d^3-35d^2+134d-47=0 (irrational)
 *   3-machine boundary: d = 1/5 (rational!)
 *   The network topology constraint produces a SIMPLER boundary.
 *
 * INSTANCE: d = 3/20, h = h*(3/20).
 */

/* Instance dn=3/20: av=1+dn=23/20, bv=(1+3dn)/4=29/80, hv=1/5 */
Definitions
  Real dn = 3/20;
  Real av = 23/20;
  Real bv = 29/80;
  Real hv = 1/5;
End.

ProgramVariables
  Real da; Real db; Real w1; Real w2; Real w3;
  Real s1; Real c1; Real s2; Real c2;
End.

Problem
  s1^2+c1^2=1 & s2^2+c2^2=1 & c1>=4/5 & c2>=4/5 &
  w1^2+w2^2+w3^2+2*(1-c1)+2*(1-c2)
    +hv*(s1^2+s2^2)+av*(w1*s1-w3*s2)+bv*w2*(s1-s2) < 1/25
  ->
  [{da'=w1, db'=w2,
    w1'=-w1-s1,
    w2'=dn*w2+s1-s2,
    w3'=-w3+s2,
    s1'=c1*(w1-w2), c1'=-s1*(w1-w2),
    s2'=c2*(w2-w3), c2'=-s2*(w2-w3)
    & s1^2+c1^2=1 & s2^2+c2^2=1 & c1>=4/5 & c2>=4/5}]
  w1^2+w2^2+w3^2+2*(1-c1)+2*(1-c2)
    +hv*(s1^2+s2^2)+av*(w1*s1-w3*s2)+bv*w2*(s1-s2) < 1/25
End.

Tactic "Proof"
  implyR(1);
  dI(1)
End.

End.
